## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to craft a robust, end-to-end evaluation pipeline for multilingual policy-faithfulness in a high-stakes financial setting, with versioned source control and drift monitoring.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual claim extraction and anchor mapping
- Versioned source citations and live policy integration
- Drift detection and change management across monthly updates

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal citation check
function checkCitation(claim, citation, policyDB) {
  const live = policyDB.lookup(citation.version, citation.id);
  return live && live.text.includes(claim.anchor);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical RAG implementation skills and understanding of how chunking affects retrieval quality - critical for SAP's document-heavy use cases.

## Expected Answer
Strong candidates mention: 1) Hierarchical chunking respecting document structure, 2) Token overlap (200-300 tokens) to preserve context, 3) Variable chunk sizes based on content density, 4) Metadata preservation (section titles, page numbers), 5) Testing different chunk sizes for optimal retrieval.

## Code Example
```typescript
function chunkDocument(text: string, maxTokens: number = 500) {
  const sections = text.split(/\n(?=#{1,3}\s)/); // Split by headers
  const chunks = [];

  for (const section of sections) {
    const sentences = section.split('. ');
    let currentChunk = '';

    for (let i = 0; i < sentences.length; i++) {
      const testChunk = currentChunk + sentences[i] + '. ';
      if (countTokens(testChunk) > maxTokens) {
        chunks.push(currentChunk.trim());
        currentChunk = sentences[i - 2] + '. ' + sentences[i - 1] + '. '; // Overlap
      } else {
        currentChunk = testChunk;
      }
    }
    chunks.push(currentChunk.trim());
  }
  return chunks;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle code blocks or tables in technical documents?
- What metrics would you use to evaluate chunking effectiveness?
- How does chunk size impact embedding quality and retrieval speed?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to implement a minimal retrieval loop that works with embeddings, chunking, and a vector-like store, while considering multilingual routing and update freshness.

## Key Concepts

- In-memory vector store
- Text chunking with overlap
- Embedding generation
- Cosine similarity search
- Multilingual handling
- Update freshness and caching

## Code Example

```javascript
